---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import { LINKS, BROWSERS } from '../config';
import { facts } from '../lib/privacy';
---
<Doc title="Install" lead={LINKS.chromeStore ? 'Add RoFit to Chrome in one click, or load it from source.' : 'RoFit isn’t on the Chrome Web Store yet. Here is how to run it today, and what to expect.'}>
  {LINKS.chromeStore && <p><a class="btn btn-curtain" href={LINKS.chromeStore} rel="noopener">Add to Chrome</a></p>}
  {!LINKS.chromeStore && <p class="callout"><strong>Honest status:</strong> there is no store listing to click yet. The steps below load the real extension straight from its source. When a listing exists, this page will lead with a normal install button.</p>}

  <h2>Which browsers</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Browser</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>{BROWSERS.chrome.name} {facts.minChrome}+</td><td>Built and tested. This is the supported browser.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Edge, Brave and other Chromium browsers</td><td>Should load the same build, since it uses the same extension format. Not separately tested or listed.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Firefox</td><td>Not available. There is no Firefox build yet.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Safari, phones and tablets</td><td>Not available.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Load it from source</h2>
  <p>You need Node.js and Git. RoFit has no accounts and needs no keys.</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Get the code from <a href={LINKS.github} rel="noopener">the GitHub repository</a> (download it as a ZIP, or <code>git clone</code>).</li>
    <li>In that folder, run <code>npm ci</code>, then <code>npm run build</code>. On Windows you can double-click <code>setup.bat</code> instead; it does both and walks you through the next step.</li>
    <li>Open <code>chrome://extensions</code> and switch on <strong>Developer mode</strong> (top right).</li>
    <li>Choose <strong>Load unpacked</strong> and pick the <code>dist</code> folder that the build created.</li>
    <li>Open any profile on roblox.com. An <strong>Outfits</strong> tab appears next to About and Creations.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Chrome may remind you at startup about developer-mode extensions. That is normal for anything not installed from the store.</p>

  <h2>Check what you installed</h2>
  <p>On <code>chrome://extensions</code>, open RoFit’s <em>Details</em> and look at <em>Permissions</em> and <em>Site access</em>. They should match the <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a> exactly: Roblox’s six read-only API hosts, plus storage, a daily cleanup alarm and the active tab.</p>

  <h2>Updating and removing</h2>
  <p>Updates from source are manual: pull the new code, rebuild, then press the reload icon on RoFit’s card. To remove it, use <em>Remove</em> on the same card; that also deletes everything RoFit stored.</p>

  <h2>Trouble?</h2>
  <p>See the <a href="/guides/no-outfits">guide on profiles with no outfits</a> or the <a href="/support">support page</a>.</p>
</Doc>
